FILE: app/src/globe-tilt.ts
```ts
import type { GeospatialCamera } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import { setGeospatialOrientation } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function tiltGlobeCamera(camera: GeospatialCamera, pitch: number): void {
    // Remove the pitch-disabled radius scale so the tilt is honored at any
    // zoom level (including fully zoomed out) and persists when the camera
    // later moves nearer to or farther from the globe.
    camera.limits.pitchDisabledRadiusScale = null;

    // Set only the pitch; yaw, radius, and center are left unchanged.
    setGeospatialOrientation(camera, { pitch });
}
```

I set `pitchDisabledRadiusScale` to `null` so the pitch is not clamped at any zoom level, then called `setGeospatialOrientation` with only the `pitch` field to apply the tilt while leaving zoom, heading, and centre untouched. The one thing I'm not 100% certain of is whether `setGeospatialOrientation` with a partial `GeospatialOrientation` object (only `pitch` provided) strictly leaves the other fields as-is — the type marks them all optional, which strongly implies it, but I can't verify the implementation since the library isn't on this machine.
